1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,000
Meet ModelDuck. A local GGUF model server and coding-model tuner that runs entirely on your machine.

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:16,000
No cloud account. No telemetry. Just serve the model, and tune it for code.

3
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Cloud coding assistants send your code away, cost money per token, and change answers when the vendor changes the model. ModelDuck keeps weights, prompts, and settings on your computer.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:01:06,000
Drop a GGUF file in a folder, import by path, or download a curated model from Hugging Face with pinned SHA-256 and resumable downloads. From half-gig Qwen starters up to 7B Mistral, ModelDuck shows real memory fit before you load.

5
00:00:40,000 --> 00:01:38,000
It serves a drop-in OpenAI-compatible API — models, chat completions, completions, with streaming — on loopback only, with keys, LAN mode, and CORS. Point ChatDuck, our static client, or any OpenAI SDK at localhost 4141, and chat.

6
00:00:58,000 --> 00:02:12,000
Here is the unfair advantage: a 262-item coding suite. Our own code, multi-file, bug-fix, comprehension and long-context recall questions, plus 20 public HumanEval and MBPP tasks, shown separately so contamination never hides.

7
00:01:14,000 --> 00:02:46,000
Bench and Tune finds the best settings for each installed model, on your hardware. Pick tasks, see quick and full time estimates from measured pace, hit Quick pass, pause, reorder a durable queue, or run it in the background.

8
00:01:32,000 --> 00:03:20,000
Five stages, in order: device, CPU or GPU measured. Quality, largest context and KV cache that fits. Speed, threads, batch, flash. Then sampling and prompt per task. A setting changes only on a clear paired gain.

9
00:01:48,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Watch it live: the setting being tried, candidate table, provisional preset, and every decision logged. A value that falls far behind stops early. Stop anywhere — each step is saved and applied.

10
00:02:04,000 --> 00:04:22,000
The result is a profile per model: device, stage progress, right answers per task. Open one to see the measured load shape and per-task settings — exportable as a checked recipe.

11
00:02:18,000 --> 00:04:48,000
Every run is kept — request, outcome, answers, pace. Recommended for this PC ranks installed models by measured answers and speed, not guesses.

12
00:02:30,000 --> 00:05:10,000
Quality is gated. Tune-gate fails if a task loses more than one item. Presets fill the form but never apply themselves until both phases pass.

13
00:02:40,000 --> 00:05:32,000
Vanilla UI, no build, no CDN. Light and dark, mobile-friendly. Loopback-only, Host and Origin checks, GGUF header guard, atomic writes.

14
00:02:52,000 --> 00:05:52,000
ModelDuck: serve the model, tune the code, keep it yours. Free for personal use. Try Qwen half-B in under a minute.
